# The canonical example, with a real implementation beside it.
login(email, password) -> session | wrong | locked
  !db !hash
  : known is a user that exists and is not locked; locked_acct is locked
  : an unknown email and a bad password give the same outcome on purpose
  (known, right) ok
  (known, bad_pw) wrong
  (unknown, any) wrong
  (locked_acct, right) locked
  ? the password check runs before the lock check, so lock state cannot leak
